{
 "duration": 26.639,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Nora ran out of water an hour from the car, so she ate a handful of snow.",
   "start": 0.4,
   "end": 4.75
  },
  {
   "text": "Soon she was colder than before.",
   "start": 5.35,
   "end": 6.981
  },
  {
   "text": "Your body burns its own heat to melt snow, and a handful is barely a sip of water.",
   "start": 7.581,
   "end": 12.397
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the fix.",
   "start": 12.997,
   "end": 13.924
  },
  {
   "text": "Carry enough water for the whole hike, keep the bladder inside your pack against your back, and sip at every break, even when you're not thirsty.",
   "start": 14.324,
   "end": 22.283
  },
  {
   "text": "Nora finished warm.",
   "start": 22.883,
   "end": 23.983
  },
  {
   "text": "Save this before your next winter hike.",
   "start": 24.583,
   "end": 26.439
  }
 ],
